        "timestamp": 1775839405,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Trump harbors an unexplained sympathy for Vladimir Putin', Ukrainian analyst says Europe Issued on: 10/04/2026 - 18:43 Ukrainian leadership on April 8 hailed the two-week ceasefire reached between the U.S. and Iran but stressed it is time to pressure Russia to end its war in Ukraine as well. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, says that the reluctance of Donald Trump to strongarm Russia into ending the war raises questions about the nature of the relationship between Trump and Vladimir Putin. Hungary: Is Viktor Orban Russia's 'Trojan horse' in the EU? 10/04/2026 Europe France plans 36 billion euro boost to rearmament, nuclear deterrent expansion 08/04/2026 Europe EU farm fraud scandal rocks Greek government, PM urges swift action 07/04/2026 Europe French nationals leave Iran after more than three years in detention 07/04/2026 Europe European Commissioner Síkela announces 'new approach' for global health 07/04/2026 Health Manlio Graziano: 'Europe still needs the US but they know they cannot trust Americans anymore' 07/04/2026 Europe 'Vladimir Putin absolutely nervous' about Hungary's election, expert says 06/04/2026 Europe Russia says 'highly likely' that Ukraine planted explosives near gas pipeline 06/04/2026 Europe Explosives found by pipeline to Hungary: PM Orban claims sabotage 06/04/2026 Europe"
